# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and fill in the values.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser.

# Google Maps JavaScript API key — the BASEMAP of the Route planner and the
# trip maps. A browser key by design: it is baked into the bundle and read by
# anyone, so restrict it in the Google Cloud console to this app's HTTP
# referrers (http://localhost:5173/* for dev, plus the production origin) and
# to the Maps JavaScript API only. Without it the maps show a "key not set"
# notice; the HGV overlay (HERE's map) still works.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=

# Routing, truck restrictions, geocoding and the HGV basemap stay HERE, and the
# HERE API key lives SERVER-SIDE only (server/.env → HERE_API_KEY). The browser
# fetches it at runtime from the auth-gated /api/here/config endpoint, so there
# is intentionally no VITE_HERE_* var here and that key is never baked into
# the frontend bundle.
